NNAAMMEE
     cchhkkggrrpp — check the syntax of the group file

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     cchhkkggrrpp [--qq] [_g_r_o_u_p_f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The cchhkkggrrpp utility scans the given file or, failing that, the system-wide
     group file for errors.  Specifically, it checks that every non-blank,
     non-comment entry is composed of four colon-separated fields, that none
     of them contains whitespace, and that the third field (the group ID) is
     numeric.  It will also check for invalid characters in the group names
     and group members.  The following options are available:

     --qq      This option disables printing of text when the group format is
             correct.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/group  group database file

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The cchhkkggrrpp utility returns EX_DATAERR if errors were found in the group
     file, and EX_OK otherwise.

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     For each error found, cchhkkggrrpp will print an error message containing the
     name of the file being scanned and the line number on which the error was
     found.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     getgrent(3), group(5)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The cchhkkggrrpp utility appeared in FreeBSD 3.0.

